{
  "id": "anticipatory-grief",
  "term": "anticipatory grief",
  "definition": "Anticipatory grief is grief that a person with a life-threatening illness, or that person’s caregiver, can experience before an actual death or other loss has happened. It involves grief symptoms arising in response to the serious illness itself.",
